// Diagnostics stage 2b fixture (CLAUDE.md §8): a PARSE error in a file that ALSO carries
// `import std...` lines. The imports are the whole point -- the driver blanks each of them
// to spaces and keeps the newline (stage 2a), so both the byte offset and the line count
// survive preprocessing and the `-->` header can name THIS file with a line number that is
// the user's own, not a line of the ~142 KB concatenated bundle.
//
// ONE mistake, on line 18: Rust/Go-style brace struct-literal syntax, which AXIOM spells
// `Point(x: 1, y: 2)`. Chosen over a dangling-operator shape because the offending TOKEN is
// on the offending LINE, so the asserted line number is the line a reader would point at.
import std.string
import std.io

struct Point:
    x: i64
    y: i64

fn main() -> i32:
    let p = Point{x: 1, y: 2}
    return 42
